{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774113920,"nonce":"Rw/igzkBNVZC2MErRWKFVK247HQ=","title":"Chat blinker timer resets on tab navigation instead of tracking actual agent activity start","message":"The \"responding\" blinker/timer in the Chat tab restarts its counter when the user navigates away and back. It should track elapsed time since the agent actually started working, not since the view was mounted. The timer state needs to persist across tab switches (store the start timestamp in component state that survives unmount, or derive it from stream events).\n\nRelated: the blinker should only be visible when the agent is actually doing something, not always.","files":null}]}